{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_011CdUR2wnQSR6Fdk1idGsVa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MVX4UHorQgLaFLQL4w2W5T","name":"Skill","input":{"skill":"ppt-master","args":"Create a 12–15 slide executive presentation deck for Northwind Logistics Q3 FY26 Quarterly Business Review. Use action titles (each title states the finding, not just the topic). The deck must stand alone without a presenter — high information density, tables and data preserved exactly. Write all output files to /Users/brycewang/Documents/GitHub/many-ppt-skills/benchmark/results/run-01/ppt-master/02-quarterly-review/rep-01/workspace/\n\nContent:\n\n### Headline\nQ3 revenue reached $47.2M, up 12.4% year over year, but gross margin compressed 180 bps on fuel and contract-labor costs.\n\n### Revenue by segment\n| Segment | Q3 FY26 | Q3 FY25 | YoY |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\n| Freight brokerage | $24.1M | $20.8M | +15.9% |\n| Warehousing | $13.6M | $12.9M | +5.4% |\n| Last-mile delivery | $7.9M | $6.4M | +23.4% |\n| Customs & compliance | $1.6M | $1.9M | −15.8% |\n| **Total** | **$47.2M** | **$42.0M** | **+12.4%** |\n\n### Quarterly revenue trend (8 quarters, $M)\n| Quarter | Revenue |\n|---|---:|\n| Q4 FY24 | 36.1 |\n| Q1 FY25 | 37.8 |\n| Q2 FY25 | 39.9 |\n| Q3 FY25 | 42.0 |\n| Q4 FY25 | 41.2 |\n| Q1 FY26 | 43.5 |\n| Q2 FY26 | 45.1 |\n| Q3 FY26 | 47.2 |\n\n### Margin\nGross margin fell from 31.2% to 29.4%. Two drivers:\n- Fuel — up 14% per mile against a flat contracted rate card. Impact: −110 bps.\n- Contract labor — peak-season warehouse staffing 22% above plan. Impact: −70 bps.\nOperating margin held at 8.1% because SG&A grew only 3.2% against 12.4% revenue growth.\n\n### Customer concentration is improving\nTop-10 customer share fell from 44% to 38% year over year — the fourth consecutive quarter of decline. Net new logos: 31, against 18 in Q3 FY25.\nChurn by count was 4.2%; churn by revenue was 2.1%, meaning the accounts we lost were smaller than average.\n\n### Last-mile is the growth engine but not yet profitable\nLast-mile grew 23.4% and now represents 16.7% of revenue, up from 15.2%.\nSegment contribution margin remains −3.4%, improving from −7.9% a year ago.\nBreak-even is projected in Q2 FY27 at current trajectory.\n\n### Headcount\n| Function | Q3 FY26 | Change QoQ |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| Operations | 812 | +34 |\n| Engineering | 96 | +11 |\n| Sales & marketing | 143 | +6 |\n| G&A | 71 | −2 |\n| **Total** | **1,122** | **+49** |\n\n### Risks\n1. Fuel exposure is unhedged beyond Q1 FY27. A further 10% move costs an estimated $1.8M annualized.\n2. Warehouse lease renewals in Memphis and Reno land in Q4 FY26, covering 340k sq ft at rates last set in 2021.\n3. Customs segment decline is structural, not cyclical — two clients insourced.\n\n### Asks\n- Approve $2.4M capex for Reno automation, targeting a 15-month payback.\n- Approve fuel hedging through Q4 FY27 at up to 60% of projected volume.\n- Approve 8 incremental engineering roles to accelerate the last-mile routing rebuild.\n\n### Q4 Outlook\nRevenue guidance $48.5M–$50.0M. Gross margin expected to recover 60–90 bps as peak-season contract labor rolls off."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1735,"cache_read_input_tokens":22043,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1735},"output_tokens":21,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"62f913d3-8d79-4b80-89f0-e9ab856e709b","uuid":"8223ddd3-3e98-4d4d-94c4-08da90ddba24","request_id":"req_011CdUR2vqMZvbgkb4o1xn5c"}
