{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PeYgy2nHtGWyfKxFyD4j2m","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Mode: pyramid\n2\t\n3\tConclusion-first argumentation. State the answer, then support it with mutually-exclusive, collectively-exhaustive evidence — every claim earns its place, every number carries a comparison. For audiences who want the result before the process: executives, boards, investors, decision-makers.\n4\t\n5\t---\n6\t\n7\t## 1. Narrative skeleton\n8\t\n9\t**Conclusion first**: the page title *is* the conclusion, not a label. The body develops the supporting arguments beneath it.\n10\t\n11\tSCQA opening, pyramid body:\n12\t\n13\t| Stage | Role | Where |\n14\t|---|---|---|\n15\t| Situation | establish shared context | cover / first 1-2 pages |\n16\t| Complication | the tension / problem | early pages |\n17\t| Question | the implicit question to resolve | transition |\n18\t| Answer | the recommendation, developed MECE | all body pages |\n19\t\n20\t**Assertion titles** — write the finding, not the topic:\n21\t\n22\t| Weak (topic) | Strong (assertion) |\n23\t|---|---|\n24\t| \"Market Overview\" | \"Domestic market grows 23% YoY, outpacing the global average\" |\n25\t| \"Challenges\" | \"Three structural contradictions block scaled deployment\" |\n26\t| \"Our Solution\" | \"Three-phase path: Focus, Expand, Scale\" |\n27\t\n28\t**Data never stands alone** — every figure pairs with a comparison (prior period / benchmark / competitor / target / rank) and a \"so what\". A bare number is an incomplete thought in this mode.\n29\t\n30\t**MECE** — when decomposing (drivers, segments, options), branches are mutually exclusive and collectively exhaustive; parts sum to the whole (or label \"Other\").\n31\t\n32\t---\n33\t\n34\t## 2. Page-structure tendencies\n35\t\n36\t- Title (the conclusion) → one-line takeaway → supporting evidence beneath.\n37\t- Each body page answers one question and states its own one-sentence conclusion.\n38\t- Decomposition pages (driver tree / MECE breakdown / 2×2 matrix) carry the analytical load.\n39\t- Source attribution on every data page.\n40\t\n41\t> Page structure is a tendency, not a coordinate template. Card / tree / chart / KPI geometry lives in [`templates/charts/`](../../templates/charts/) — adapt those skeletons, do not reinvent. This mode decides *what argument each page makes*, not pixel positions.\n42\t\n43\t---\n44\t\n45\t## 3. Speaker-notes register\n46\t\n47\tConclusion-driven: the first sentence of each page's notes is the takeaway, then 2-3 supporting facts in flowing prose. Composed, authoritative. Every number paired with its comparison in the same sentence (\"23% — nearly double the industry's 12%\"). Spell percentages as words where the spoken form reads more naturally. (Common framework: [`executor-notes.md`](../executor-notes.md) §1.)\n48\t\n49\t---\n50\t\n51\t## 4. Page skeleton example\n52\t\n53\t```\n54\tTitle:    \"Retention, not acquisition, now drives growth\"   ← the conclusion\n55\tTakeaway: one line — \"CAC up 40% YoY, yet repurchase lifted 60% of revenue growth\"\n56\tBody:     3 MECE arguments, each with one contextualized datum\n57\tFooter:   Source: … | page #\n58\t```\n59\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"62f913d3-8d79-4b80-89f0-e9ab856e709b","uuid":"f512b790-184d-4c7c-9f3a-a28c0821b70a","timestamp":"2026-07-28T12:04:24.298Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/brycewang/Documents/GitHub/many-ppt-skills/benchmark/results/run-01/ppt-master/02-quarterly-review/rep-01/workspace/.claude/skills/ppt-master/references/modes/pyramid.md","content":"# Mode: pyramid\n\nConclusion-first argumentation. State the answer, then support it with mutually-exclusive, collectively-exhaustive evidence — every claim earns its place, every number carries a comparison. For audiences who want the result before the process: executives, boards, investors, decision-makers.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Narrative skeleton\n\n**Conclusion first**: the page title *is* the conclusion, not a label. The body develops the supporting arguments beneath it.\n\nSCQA opening, pyramid body:\n\n| Stage | Role | Where |\n|---|---|---|\n| Situation | establish shared context | cover / first 1-2 pages |\n| Complication | the tension / problem | early pages |\n| Question | the implicit question to resolve | transition |\n| Answer | the recommendation, developed MECE | all body pages |\n\n**Assertion titles** — write the finding, not the topic:\n\n| Weak (topic) | Strong (assertion) |\n|---|---|\n| \"Market Overview\" | \"Domestic market grows 23% YoY, outpacing the global average\" |\n| \"Challenges\" | \"Three structural contradictions block scaled deployment\" |\n| \"Our Solution\" | \"Three-phase path: Focus, Expand, Scale\" |\n\n**Data never stands alone** — every figure pairs with a comparison (prior period / benchmark / competitor / target / rank) and a \"so what\". A bare number is an incomplete thought in this mode.\n\n**MECE** — when decomposing (drivers, segments, options), branches are mutually exclusive and collectively exhaustive; parts sum to the whole (or label \"Other\").\n\n---\n\n## 2. Page-structure tendencies\n\n- Title (the conclusion) → one-line takeaway → supporting evidence beneath.\n- Each body page answers one question and states its own one-sentence conclusion.\n- Decomposition pages (driver tree / MECE breakdown / 2×2 matrix) carry the analytical load.\n- Source attribution on every data page.\n\n> Page structure is a tendency, not a coordinate template. Card / tree / chart / KPI geometry lives in [`templates/charts/`](../../templates/charts/) — adapt those skeletons, do not reinvent. This mode decides *what argument each page makes*, not pixel positions.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Speaker-notes register\n\nConclusion-driven: the first sentence of each page's notes is the takeaway, then 2-3 supporting facts in flowing prose. Composed, authoritative. Every number paired with its comparison in the same sentence (\"23% — nearly double the industry's 12%\"). Spell percentages as words where the spoken form reads more naturally. (Common framework: [`executor-notes.md`](../executor-notes.md) §1.)\n\n---\n\n## 4. Page skeleton example\n\n```\nTitle:    \"Retention, not acquisition, now drives growth\"   ← the conclusion\nTakeaway: one line — \"CAC up 40% YoY, yet repurchase lifted 60% of revenue growth\"\nBody:     3 MECE arguments, each with one contextualized datum\nFooter:   Source: … | page #\n```\n","numLines":59,"startLine":1,"totalLines":59}}}
